+# Taskboard acceptance project
+
+This is a disposable project on the remote execution host. Use only ordinary
+SSH in this task-owned worktree; no host administration is needed.
+Use Python's standard library, retain existing tests, and commit each task
+locally. Do not push. Work only on this fixture, not real business directories.
+
+The CLI is `python3 taskboard.py --db PATH COMMAND`. Existing commands add,
+complete and list tasks. State is a JSON object containing `next_id` and `tasks`.
+
+Feature task: implement `export --format csv [--tag TAG]`. Output UTF-8 CSV with
+LF line endings and columns `id,title,done,tags`. Sort by numeric ID, encode
+done as lowercase true/false, join sorted unique tags with semicolons, and use
+correct CSV escaping. Missing or empty databases produce only the header.
+Export is read-only and must not create the database. This task must not alter
+the storage/write implementation; a separate task covers storage integrity.
+
+Storage bug task: concurrent successful mutations must retain every task and
+allocate unique monotonically increasing IDs. Readers must never see a partial
+JSON write. Failed or interrupted writes must preserve the previous database.
+Preserve existing database permissions; new databases should be private (0600).
+Do not silently reset corrupt input or weaken acceptance tests.
+
+Run `nix develop -c python3 -m unittest -v`; add useful regressions in new files. All diagnosis,
+edits, tests and Git actions must run through SSH on this host. Do not copy the
+project to OVH to implement or test it. Do not inspect addresses, routing,
+credentials or proxy configuration. Report infrastructure failures; do not
+change the target or bypass the managed SSH interface.
